2026-11-07T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-2477) 'Can a corner be placed on the chart correctly even when the id painted next to it is wrong?
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD2477  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-2477) 'Treat the board as a spatially coded pattern instead of a set of independently-read tags: detect corners without trusting their ids, place each corner on the chart by voting over offsets, rotations and instances, and recover unread markers from their read neighbours. `predict_neighbours.py` already exists for this but was never run, and was left out of the earlier pull requests.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2477  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-2477) 'Run `predict_neighbours.py` against planted gates before trusting any measurement from it.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2477  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-2477) 'Ship three gates ahead of any measurement, each with its own planted-defect control:
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2477  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-2477) '- A planted wrong offset must lose the vote, so one bad candidate never outvotes the consistent majority.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2477  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-2477) '- A blank pattern (no corners detected) gives nothing back, rather than a false placement.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2477  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-2477) '- The UV pass marks every assignment right or wrong, with no assignment left unjudged. Once those three gates pass, measure corners placed, wrong placements, and markers recovered that tag decoding alone misses, and report those three numbers together, not separately.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2477  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-2477) '- RFD66606-2467, the dead-on gate this recovery path feeds markers back into.
 # tags: rfd:related
